<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Two capability strings, and only two. WKWebView will not hand
       `getUserMedia` a capture device unless the bundle carries the matching
       usage description, and iOS terminates the process outright if the string
       is missing at the moment of capture, so an app that hosts a livestream
       and omits these does not degrade — it crashes. free2z hosts Cloudflare
       RealtimeKit rooms: a host publishes camera and microphone the moment the
       room opens (`src/features/live/Stage.tsx` initialises with
       `audio: ticket.as === "host"`, `video: ticket.as === "host"`), and the
       RealtimeKit meeting UI offers every participant the same two toggles.
       Both strings therefore describe a thing the app actually does.

       Nothing else is claimed. free2z has no wallet seed and no messaging keys
       (#904), so there is no NSFaceIDUsageDescription; it reads no contacts,
       no location and no photo library, and adding a usage string for a
       capability the app never exercises is how an App Store reviewer is told
       a lie. `wallet/free2z/scripts/release-identity.mjs` fails the build if
       any of those appear here. -->
  <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
  <string>free2z uses the camera when you host or join a live stream.</string>
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>free2z uses the microphone when you host or join a live stream.</string>
  <key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleURLName</key>
      <string>cash.free2z.free2z</string>
      <key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
      <array>
        <string>cash.free2z.free2z</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
